course: dictionary
lesson: 11019
title: Watery: many meanings, one clue
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Watery comes from water, so it always has something to do with water. But it does not always mean wet. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The honey left too watery can go mouldy» means it has too much water in it, so it is thin and runny.
explain: «Through the window came a watery sun, pale and weak in the winter sky.» The sun is not wet at all. Watery describes its light. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Pale would fit, so watery can mean pale and weak in colour or light.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it. «Her watery eyes stung in the cold wind» means her eyes were full of tears, not that they were thin or pale.
fact: Watery means containing too much water, full of water or wet, or pale and weak in colour or light.
fact: «Watery soup» is thin and weak, because it has too much water and not enough flavour.
fact: Snailfish have soft, «watery» bodies, so the pressure of the deep sea does not crush them.
fact: «A watery grave» means a grave in the sea, where someone has drowned.
exercise: «Honey left too watery can go mouldy.» What does watery mean here? | Cold and hard | Very sweet and sticky | Full of bees | *Containing too much water, so it is thin
exercise: «Through the window came a watery sun.» What does watery describe? | Wet and dripping rain | *Pale and weak light | A loud noise | Hot and bright light
exercise: Nadia says «watery eyes» means eyes that are dry and sore. Is she right? | No, watery eyes are full of water or tears | No, they are closed | *Yes, they are dry and sore | Yes, they are very bright
test: «The soup was so watery that it tasted of nothing.» What does watery mean? | *Thin and weak, with too much water | Thick and creamy | Hot and spicy | Sour
test: Which meaning fits «a watery grave»? | A grave with flowers on it | A grave on a hill | *Connected with water, such as drowning at sea | A grave dug in soft mud
exam: Mia says watery only means wet. Is she completely right? | Yes, because it comes from water | Yes, it only ever means wet | *No, it can also mean thin and weak, or pale and weak in light | No, it means happy
